  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Drier cooler weather returns today and continues\ninto early next week.\n\nHigh pressure will build in today, driving cooler and drier air\nacross the region into the middle of the week. An upper-level \ntrough will linger overhead, though it will only yield a few \nfair- weather clouds during the afternoon hours. Mostly clear \nskies will ensure zero chance of rain through Wednesday.\n\nTemperatures will run cooler than normal through Tuesday, with \nhighs settling in the 70s west of the Blue Ridge and the 80s to \nthe east. Nighttime temperatures will drop into the crisp 50s. \nBy Thursday, the primary high-pressure system will finally break\ndown, allowing the Bermuda High to slide over the region and \ndraw a steady stream of muggy moisture back into the area.",
